
<article class="about-article">
<h1>About lhwx.org</h1>

<p>Positioned on Lea Hill in Auburn, WA, this weather station is powered by an Ambient Weather WH65B. Data samples are taken every 16 seconds and published live to this site.</p>

<p>This station tracks the following weather measurements:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Temperature (ambient air temperature)</li>
  <li>Feels like (calculation using a combination of wind chill/humidity/heat index/solar)</li>
  <li>Humidity</li>
  <li>Barometric pressure</li>
  <li>Wind</li>
  <li>Direction</li>
  <li>Speed</li>
  <li>Rainfall</li>
  <li>UV (by way of solar irradiance and lux)</li>
</ul>

<p>Everything else is recorded and interpolated using software.</p>

