<h2>Technical details</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Weather station: Ecowitt WH65B</li>
  <li>Data capture: Ecowitt GW11000</li>
  <li>Data is measured in metric units (Celsius, mm, etc.) and converted to imperial units (Fahrenheit, inches, etc.) for display. Pressure is captured in hPa/millibars and displayed the same.</li>
  <li>All timestamps are recorded in UTC and coverted to <code>America/Los_Angeles</code> for display.</li>
  <li>Forecasts: The <%= link_to "OpenWeatherMap API", "https://openweathermap.org/api?utm_source=lhwx.org&utm_medium=referral", target: "_blank" %>, retrieved every 30 minutes.</li>
  <li>Air quality: <%= link_to "AirNow", "https://www.airnow.gov/", target: "_blank" %> HourlyAQObs for the Auburn 29th St monitor (EPA AQI / PM2.5), retrieved hourly.</li>
  <li>Backend: data is captured through a custom <%= link_to "Rust application", "https://github.com/johlym/wxlistener", target: "_blank" %> and forwarded to this site via an HTTP endpoint.</li>
  <li>Frontend: this site is built using Ruby on Rails. Data is stored in a PostgreSQL database.</li>
  <li>Hosting: <%= link_to "Heroku", "https://www.heroku.com?utm_source=lhwx.org&utm_medium=referral", target: "_blank" %></li>
</ul>

<h2>Some semi-relevant details:</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Number of weather measurements: <%= number_with_delimiter(@weather_measurement_count) %></li>
  <li>First measurement: <%= @first_weather_measurement.reading_date_time.in_time_zone("America/Los_Angeles").strftime("%b %d, %Y @ %I:%M %p") %></li>
</ul>
